# Cameras for the Nanjing run: 400 x 400 x 80 at 5 m, so a 2000 x 2000 x 400 m
# box -- 100 m taller than the Manchester defaults assume, with buildings to
# 337.5 m.
#
# ALL THREE SHARE ONE AZIMUTH, DUE SOUTH, and that is the whole design. It is
# manhattan.env's rule applied to a different heading: place every camera
# perpendicular to the plume's axis and the plume travels left to right in all
# three panels, so they read as one event seen three ways. Here the wind blows
# due EAST (-bearing 270), so perpendicular is due south -- no street-grid
# measurement needed, unlike Manhattan, where the axis had to be recovered from
# the geometry.
#
# THE FOCUS IS PER PANEL, AND GETTING THAT WRONG COST A WHOLE RENDER. The
# source sits at j = 60, so the plume runs along y = 300 m, well south of
# centre. For the SKYLINE the domain centre is right and the plume line is
# wrong: focusing on the plume moves the camera 700 m further out, the near
# ground plane then fills the bottom third and the city shrinks, where the
# centre puts the plume in the FOREGROUND, partly behind the near towers, which
# reads as depth. For the other two it is the reverse, and the first build of
# this file used the centre for all three: the plan view then ran the plume
# along its bottom edge, half out of frame, and the low oblique showed it as a
# thin strip under an empty sky. Both are focused on the plume line here. One
# focus for three panels is not a simplification -- it is two wrong panels.
#
# -fov is the VERTICAL angle. At 2800 m the skyline panel's 1160 x 940 gives
# 1981 m of horizontal coverage against a 2000 m box, i.e. about 1 % clipped at
# the two ends -- deliberate, since pulling back far enough to clear it wastes
# the frame on sky. Elevation 16 degrees was picked against 10 and 24: at 10 the
# city is a thin band with no street layout, at 24 it stops being a skyline.

FOC=997.5,997.5,112

# skyline sweep, 1160 x 940 -- the whole 2 km broadside, 2800 m out at 16 deg
CAM_H=997.5,-1694.0,883.8
FOC_H=997.5,997.5,112
FOV_H=32

# low oblique, 750 x 420 -- 1200 m out at 6 deg, on the plume's own line, so
# the plume is seen in PROFILE between the towers rather than above them
CAM_E=997.5,-893.4,245.4
FOC_E=997.5,300.0,120
FOV_E=34

# plan view, 750 x 510 -- 2800 m up at 81 deg, on the plume's line, same azimuth
CAM_G=997.5,-18.0,2825.5
FOC_G=997.5,420.0,60
FOV_G=30
